<!--

    Copyright (C) 2026 Antony Stubbs and contributors

    SpotBugs exclusions for the Java harness lane (astubbs#242; the policy is in
    docs/client-static-analysis.md). The gate itself is bound in the parent pom.

    One entry, naming one class, one method and one pattern. Every entry here is a judgement, not a
    mute: if you are adding one, write why, or fix the code.

-->
<FindBugsFilter>

    <!--
        THE SOCKET IS NEVER SERVED ON. findsecbugs wants an SSLServerSocket; this one is opened on
        the loopback address purely to have the OS allocate a port number, and it is closed inside
        the same try-with-resources before anything connects to it - the test needs a port that is
        valid and NOT listening, which is the control arm proving the sibling assertion fails for the
        reason it names rather than on any error at all. There is no traffic to encrypt.

        The wider posture is the same call astubbs/parallel-consumer#384 recorded for the sidecar's
        own tests: this listener is plaintext BY DESIGN, because loopback-only binding plus
        one-connection admission is what the sidecar offers instead of transport security, and a test
        that used TLS would be testing a listener that does not exist.

        Scoped to the one method, so any other socket opened in this module is still reported.
    -->
    <Match>
        <Class name="bz.stub.parallelconsumer.client.harness.SidecarHandshakeTest"/>
        <Method name="aSidecarThatIsNotListeningFailsDifferentlyFromOneThatRefuses"/>
        <Bug pattern="UNENCRYPTED_SERVER_SOCKET"/>
    </Match>

</FindBugsFilter>
